Z||000000||Gasolene||04-02-2001||07:42 PM||||i have no brake lights<BR>84 fiero 2m4<P>there is power at the fuse & on the brown wire at brake switch.<P>I think it is the brake switch but the fiero manual says there is a white terminal on the steering column connector that I should check for voltage before replacing the switch.<P>I don't know where this connector is, there is lots of connectors under the steering column.<P>If it is the brake switch, how do i replace it??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-02-2001||10:26 PM||||I believe the connector that you seek can be found under the steering column behind the lower column cover. It will be a white connector with several wires (7?) that go to it. It looks like a long single connector strip. You will need to check the white wire for voltage (+12 volts).<BR>You should also check the connector at the switch itself first. It can be found mounted to the brake pedal mount. There are two switches located there (if you have cruise) the wire is still white. The other wire on this plug is light blue or blue, just jumper the two together and if you have brake lights check the switch.||||reg||1
